Title: 0008-scenario-load-errors
Repository: micropoliscore
Base-Commit: 69ccf87ed72d2d2950b70cf16ef1391439bd9d48
Requires: 0007-packed-city-fields.patch
Author: aros-micropolis project
Date: 2026-09-19
Upstream-Status: candidate
Scope: Engine scenario loader on all platforms; native frontend uses isolated previews.

Problem:
  Native scenario loading constructs std::string from NULL and ignores missing or truncated city files.
Solution:
  Initialize empty strings and return a checked boolean load result. Frontends can select transactionally using a fresh simulator.
Validation:
  2026-09-19: tests/startup/run-tests.sh 60/60 with ASan/UBSan; all eight scenarios, missing and truncated city failure.
  ABIv11 guest: Tokyo preview -> Play -> sim step; both ABI builds; complete series reproduction.
  WASM build not tested.
Removal:
  Permanent correctness fix; remove when an equivalent checked loader is in the pinned upstream.

diff --git a/packages/micropolis-engine/src/fileio.cpp b/packages/micropolis-engine/src/fileio.cpp
index 3bf827d..10d0345 100644
--- a/packages/micropolis-engine/src/fileio.cpp
+++ b/packages/micropolis-engine/src/fileio.cpp
@@ -404,10 +404,10 @@ bool Micropolis::saveFile(const std::string &filename)
  * @param s Scenario to load.
  * @note \a s cannot be \c SC_NONE.
  */
-void Micropolis::loadScenario(Scenario s)
+bool Micropolis::loadScenario(Scenario s)
 {
-    std::string name = NULL;
-    std::string fname = NULL;
+    std::string name;
+    std::string fname;
 
     cityFileName = "";
 
@@ -483,7 +483,12 @@ void Micropolis::loadScenario(Scenario s)
     setSpeed(3);
     setCityTax(7);
 
-    loadFileData(fname);
+    // Native std::string cannot be constructed from NULL. Also do not
+    // announce a successful scenario after an absent/truncated city file.
+    // Callers needing transactional selection load into a fresh simulator.
+    if (!loadFileData(fname)) {
+        return false;
+    }
 
     initWillStuff();
     initFundingLevel();
@@ -493,6 +498,7 @@ void Micropolis::loadScenario(Scenario s)
     doInitialEval = false;
     doSimInit();
     didLoadScenario(s, name, fname);
+    return true;
 }
 
 
